@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each positional object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ", end="!\n")
+
+Unlike print, ``out`` does not pretty print containers, does not wrap or crop output, does not apply console markup, and does not replace emoji codes. Its output is written as plain text. It does apply a basic ``style`` and will highlight output by default; set ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+
+Output from ``out`` still passes through the console's render hooks and uses the same buffer and capture behavior as print.
+
+
